    outbox "https://discuss.systems/users/emeryberger/outbox"
    summary "<p>Professor, Computer Science, Univ. of Massachusetts Amherst. My students, collaborators, and I build innovative systems, especially focused on performance, reliability, and security -- Scalene, Coz, Hoard, and more. Among other things, I am also the creator/maintainer of <a href=&amp;#34;https://CSrankings.org&amp;#34; target=&amp;#34;_blank&amp;#34; rel=&amp;#34;nofollow noopener&amp;#34; translate=&amp;#34;no&amp;#34;><span class=&amp;#34;invisible&amp;#34;>https://</span><span class=&amp;#34;&amp;#34;>CSrankings.org</span><span class=&amp;#34;invisible&amp;#34;></span></a>.</p><p>Twitter (while it lasts): <span class=&amp;#34;h-card&amp;#34; translate=&amp;#34;no&amp;#34;><a href=&amp;#34;https://discuss.systems/@emeryberger&amp;#34; class=&amp;#34;u-url mention&amp;#34;>@<span>emeryberger</span></a></span><br />Home page: <a href=&amp;#34;https://emeryberger.com&amp;#34; target=&amp;#34;_blank&amp;#34; rel=&amp;#34;nofollow noopener&amp;#34; translate=&amp;#34;no&amp;#34;><span class=&amp;#34;invisible&amp;#34;>https://</span><span class=&amp;#34;&amp;#34;>emeryberger.com</span><span class=&amp;#34;invisible&amp;#34;></span></a><br />Lab page: <a href=&amp;#34;http://PLASMA-UMass.org&amp;#34; target=&amp;#34;_blank&amp;#34; rel=&amp;#34;nofollow noopener&amp;#34; translate=&amp;#34;no&amp;#34;><span class=&amp;#34;invisible&amp;#34;>http://</span><span class=&amp;#34;&amp;#34;>PLASMA-UMass.org</span><span class=&amp;#34;invisible&amp;#34;></span></a><br />GitHubs:<br />* <a href=&amp;#34;http://github.com/plasma-umass/&amp;#34; target=&amp;#34;_blank&amp;#34; rel=&amp;#34;nofollow noopener&amp;#34; translate=&amp;#34;no&amp;#34;><span class=&amp;#34;invisible&amp;#34;>http://</span><span class=&amp;#34;&amp;#34;>github.com/plasma-umass/</span><span class=&amp;#34;invisible&amp;#34;></span></a><br />* <a href=&amp;#34;http://github.com/emeryberger&amp;#34; target=&amp;#34;_blank&amp;#34; rel=&amp;#34;nofollow noopener&amp;#34; translate=&amp;#34;n